<div class="exhibit" aria-label="A note from the record and the ledger of changes that left it alone">
  <figure class="doc-card" data-file="canon/payment-retries.md">
    <span class="doc-label">Guarantee across owners</span>
    <p class="doc-title">A retried charge never bills twice.</p>
    <p>
      Checkout, the billing worker and the bank adapter all rely on the
      client's idempotency key: a replay returns the first result, because a
      customer was double-billed in an outage (owner). Enforced by the
      charge-replay test.
    </p>
    <p class="doc-rejects">
      No front matter, no file paths, no limits copied from code. The note
      holds only what no single module can.
    </p>
    <div class="doc-divide" role="presentation"></div>
    <span class="doc-label">And no decision record</span>
    <p>
      <strong>Postgres over an event log:</strong> the reason and the
      rejected option are in the commit body. If the owner reverses it, the
      one clause that mentions it is edited in place.
    </p>
  </figure>
  <figure class="term hero-term">
    <figcaption class="term-bar">
      <span class="term-dots" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
      <span>write trigger — what each change did to canon</span>
    </figcaption>
    <div class="term-body" tabindex="0">
      <table class="ledger">
        <caption class="sr-only">
          Four implementation changes: each row lists a change, whether it
          made a Canon sentence false, and what happened to Canon.
        </caption>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>extract retry helper</td>
            <td class="dim">nothing false</td>
            <td class="pass">canon untouched</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>rename charge module</td>
            <td class="dim">nothing false</td>
            <td class="pass">canon untouched</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>retry ceiling 3 → 5</td>
            <td class="dim">lives in code</td>
            <td class="pass">code + test only</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>adapter drops the key</td>
            <td class="flag">guarantee false</td>
            <td class="dim">note fixed, same change</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <div class="gate-line">
        <span class="pass">no checker · no stamps · no records</span>
        <span class="dim">(small by rule, not by tooling)</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </figure>
</div>
